# Architecture

## Layers (top → bottom)

Presentation → API / Dashboard → Application → Agents → Skills → Repositories → Database / External APIs

## Hard rules

- UI must not contain business logic.
- Agents must not access the database directly.
- Agents use explicit tools/skills only.
- Skills must not depend on Streamlit.
- Database access is encapsulated in repositories.
- External APIs are isolated behind ingestion/integration components.
- Schemas define boundaries between layers.
- Application services coordinate use cases.
- Domain / analytics logic remains independently testable.
- Dependencies flow inward; avoid circular imports.

## Before a new abstraction

Ask: "Does this reduce complexity?" If not, do not create it.

## Architectural violation

Flag as **ARCHITECTURAL VIOLATION** when a change breaks these boundaries.

Reference: `docs/architecture/`.
